.TH LACIS 1 "2026-11-12" "Lacis" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lacis \- map French companies, their directors and addresses into a sourced link graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lacis
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.br
.B lacis
.B \-\-version
.br
.B lacis
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lacis
starts Lacis, a desktop OSINT tool for French company data.
Starting from one company, it pulls the threads: who runs it, which other
companies those people run, who else is registered at the same address, and what
the BODACC published about each of them.
Explainable rules then flag the patterns worth a closer look.
.PP
Every fact in the graph links back to the public response it came from, with its
date and its SHA\-256 fingerprint.
Each investigation is a local SQLite database.
Nothing leaves the computer except the public requests the user triggers.
The interface is in French.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start Lacis on a fake API of fictional companies, with a temporary data
directory.
Nothing is read from or written to the real data directory.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version of Lacis and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LACIS_DATA_DIRECTORY
Directory of the investigations, instead of the default one.
.TP
.B LACIS_CONFIGURATION_DIRECTORY
Directory of the signal rules configuration, instead of the default one.
.TP
.B LACIS_LOG_DIRECTORY
Directory of the log files, instead of the default one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Lacis/Lacis/investigations/
One directory per investigation, with its database, its raw responses and its
collection log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/Lacis/Lacis.ini
Settings: window size, theme and column widths.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/Lacis/Lacis/logs/
Log files, which give the details of unexpected errors.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at
.UR https://github.com/c4seus/lacis/issues
.UE .
